F1    THE WIRING WITNESS, SCORED FIRST: the CADENCE lines. below=1 iff [QCLK] site=receiver w_us_max < the cell's shipped effective floor. It is a RESULT line and NEVER an abort -- if F1 fires every other clause is VOID and this row names the next cadence in the chain.
TIMER the SHIPPED [25,100] ms clamp is the SENDER's timer on EVERY row: RWM_QUANTILE_CLOCKS/RWM_RACK_CLOCKS/RWM_DERIVED_SWEEP are CONTAMINATION gates and RWM_W_FORM must resolve cantelli
F3    a delivered cadence below TAIL_SWEEP_MIN_US = 25 ms puts the RECEIVER's report clock AHEAD of the SENDER's backstop for the first time in this engine's history -- a stated confound on the sub-floor arms, carried on every reading taken from them
RPD   the wiring test statistic, CROSS-ENDPOINT: [FCAUSE] n (sender) / [SUCC] det (receiver)
ARM-VOID (law_n=0) is a RESULT and never an abort
BANDSCOPE the goodput abort bands apply to CTL ONLY (band_applies=1); an out-of-band TREATMENT reading is a RESULT -- it is 16.78.4's P-B
